{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3086","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3086","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3086\",\"parent_revision\":\"e7b9a288e051275e204418b97865ce322dfa435b8faaf921d726593fec3a2027\",\"root_revision\":\"e7b9a288e051275e204418b97865ce322dfa435b8faaf921d726593fec3a2027\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n`component-architecture.md`'s Content model section previously claimed `artifact_register()`\\nis \\\"the only place\\\" that computes artifact identity and writes the manifest entry. Verified\\nagainst source that this is false \u2014 there are three independent artifact-registration code\\npaths in `backlog_core`:\\n\\n- `artifact_register()` (the MCP tool, `backlog_core/server.py`) calls `publish_artifact()`\\n  (`backlog_core/artifact_manifest_store.py`), which computes `content_revision` via\\n  `hashlib.sha256` before writing the manifest entry.\\n- `_try_register_dispatch_plan_artifact()` (`backlog_core/server.py`) also calls\\n  `publish_artifact()` directly \u2014 a second caller of the same shared identity-computing owner.\\n- `_migrate_register_one()` (`backlog_core/artifact_migration.py`) does **not** go through\\n  `publish_artifact()` at all. It calls `ArtifactRegistry.register()` and\\n  `provider.set_manifest()` directly, and never computes `content_revision`.\\n\\nThe doc fix corrects the false \\\"only place\\\" claim to describe `publish_artifact()` as the\\nshared identity-computing owner both `artifact_register` and\\n`_try_register_dispatch_plan_artifact` route through. This issue tracks the underlying gap:\\nartifacts registered via `artifact_migration.py`'s migration path carry no `content_revision`,\\nwhich is inconsistent with how every other registration path establishes artifact identity.\\n\\n## Dependencies\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nNone known.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] `_migrate_register_one()` either routes through `publish_artifact()` (or an equivalent\\n      shared identity-computing helper) so migrated artifacts carry a `content_revision`, or\\n      the manifest schema documents why migration-path entries are exempt from content identity\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"ff5ad192052c638c7573ccba75c1ceb8056d70c29b2bc5588d206c8b5ed197f1\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABQIpgCg\"}"}